From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: park the DSU on PERI0_600M during a relock

What. The DSU clock mux gains its encoding 101, PERI0_600M, as a third
parent, wired from the main CCU as the CPU CCU's optional second input
"peri0-600m". When it is wired and runs at 600 MHz, the DSU's relock
notifier parks the DSU there instead of on CPU_SLOW_CLK (the 26 MHz
DCXO). probe() holds the clock enabled, so the park target cannot be gated
underneath the DSU. Without the DT input the DSU parks on the DCXO as
before.

New dependency: the CPU CCU now also consumes a main-CCU clock. Both are
platform drivers ordered by fw_devlink; the main CCU has no reference back,
so there is no cycle, but a main CCU that fails to probe now also holds
back the CPU clocks and with them cpufreq -- before this patch they waited
on the RTC CCU only.

Why. Until now nothing changed the DSU rate, so its park was never used.
The DSU devfreq driver later in this series changes it whenever the CPU
policies move. The DSU clocks the L3 cache and the snoop filter of all
eight cores; parked on the DCXO, every one of those changes would hold
the whole memory side at 26 MHz for the relock -- about 250 us for a
cluster PLL on the DCXO, most of it software running at 26 MHz.

Sources:
  - UM V1.00 5.1.10.37 (CPU_DSU_PLL_CLK_REG, 0x301c) bits 26:24:
    000/001/010 CPU_SLOW_CLK, 011 CPU_DSU_PLL/P, 100 CPU0PLL,
    101 PERI0_600M; the mux switches glitch-free and
    can be reconfigured dynamically.
  - UM 5.1.4.1: the cluster's primary source is CPU_DSU_PLL;
    its backup sources are the 26 MHz DCXO, CPU_BACK_PLL and 600 MHz. 101
    is the only one of the three the DSU mux offers besides the DCXO.
  - The park never runs the DSU faster than the rail allows: 600 MHz is
    below 780 MHz, where boot0 leaves the DSU at DCDC5's 800 mV floor.

Verified, 8 GiB board (speed bin 5), 2026-09-29, register level before this
patch existed: 780 -> 600 -> relock -> back,
repeated for 910 and 1066 MHz, 18 switches under a running system with no
kernel log line and stress-ng --verify clean after each switch. The 600 MHz
arm itself ran for the whole A/B of 2026-09-25 (6 GiB board). Builds at
W=1 with no warning; the dtb carries both clocks.

Verified on silicon through the kernel path, 8 GiB board, 6.18.54 test
kernel with the devfreq driver, 2026-09-29: probe prints "DSU parks on
PERI0_600M during a relock"; ccu_a733_park_nb_cb logs every DSU change,
median 48 us parked (5 changes, max 48.4 us); 14 816 changes in 10 min
under stress-ng --verify, failed 0, no kernel log line. The park
itself is too short to sample the mux from userspace; the DCXO park
of the DSU was never timed for comparison.

Vendor comparison: the vendor driver gives all three CPU muxes one parent
list ending in "pll-cpu-back", which for the DSU names the wrong source
for encoding 101 (it is PERI0_600M there); it never changes the DSU rate,
so it never parks it.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 .../clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-cpu-ccu.yaml  | 12 +++++-
 .../sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts         |  8 +++-
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c    | 42 +++++++++++++++----
 3 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-cpu-ccu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-cpu-ccu.yaml
index 14a17da44..069bbe686 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-cpu-ccu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/allwinner,sun60i-a733-cpu-ccu.yaml
@@ -31,12 +31,19 @@ properties:
     maxItems: 1
 
   clocks:
+    minItems: 1
     items:
       - description: Digitally Controlled Crystal Oscillator (26 MHz on the A733)
+      - description:
+          PERI0_600M from the main CCU, the DSU clock mux's encoding 101.
+          Used only as the DSU's park source while its PLL relocks; without
+          it the DSU parks on the DCXO.
 
   clock-names:
+    minItems: 1
     items:
       - const: dcxo
+      - const: peri0-600m
 
 required:
   - "#clock-cells"
@@ -49,13 +56,14 @@ additionalProperties: false
 
 examples:
   - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
     #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-rtc-ccu.h>
 
     clock-controller@8870000 {
         compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-cpu-ccu";
         reg = <0x08870000 0x3038>;
-        clocks = <&rtc_ccu CLK_RTC_DCXO>;
-        clock-names = "dcxo";
+        clocks = <&rtc_ccu CLK_RTC_DCXO>, <&ccu CLK_PLL_PERI0_600M>;
+        clock-names = "dcxo", "peri0-600m";
         #clock-cells = <1>;
     };
 
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
index 1eb2e9510..bf5db2f99 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -3172,8 +3172,12 @@ rtc_ccu: clock-controller@709015c {
 		cpupll_ccu: clock-controller@8870000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-cpu-ccu";
 			reg = <0x0 0x08870000 0x0 0x3038>;
-			clocks = <&rtc_ccu CLK_RTC_DCXO>;
-			clock-names = "dcxo";
+			/*
+			 * peri0-600m: the DSU mux's encoding 101, where the DSU
+			 * parks while its PLL relocks.
+			 */
+			clocks = <&rtc_ccu CLK_RTC_DCXO>, <&ccu CLK_PLL_PERI0_600M>;
+			clock-names = "dcxo", "peri0-600m";
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c
index 675f60993..e9a6d3d63 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-cpu.c
@@ -524,10 +524,12 @@ A733_CPU_PLL(pll_cpu_dsu_clk, "pll-cpu-dsu",
  * muxes the same parent list ending in "pll-cpu-back", which is wrong for the
  * DSU. Encoding 100 is omitted here for both: on L/B it is a tap of the
  * peripheral PLL that lives in the main CCU and would need a DT input we would
- * never select, and on the DSU it is a different source again.
+ * never select, and on the DSU it is a different source again. The DSU's 101,
+ * PERI0_600M, is a DT input ("peri0-600m") and only ever the park target of a
+ * DSU relock (see the notifiers below).
  */
 static const u8 a733_cpu_core_mux_table[] = { 0, 3, 5 };
-static const u8 a733_cpu_dsu_mux_table[] = { 0, 3 };
+static const u8 a733_cpu_dsu_mux_table[] = { 0, 3, 5 };
 
 static const struct clk_parent_data cpu_l_parents[] = {
 	{ .fw_name = "dcxo" },				/* 000 CPU_SLOW_CLK */
@@ -542,8 +544,9 @@ static const struct clk_parent_data cpu_b_parents[] = {
 };
 
 static const struct clk_parent_data cpu_dsu_parents[] = {
-	{ .fw_name = "dcxo" },
-	{ .hw = &pll_cpu_dsu_clk.common.hw },
+	{ .fw_name = "dcxo" },				/* 000 CPU_SLOW_CLK  */
+	{ .hw = &pll_cpu_dsu_clk.common.hw },		/* 011 CPU_DSU_PLL/P */
+	{ .fw_name = "peri0-600m" },			/* 101 PERI0_600M    */
 };
 
 /*
@@ -662,11 +665,20 @@ A733_CPU_MUX_NB(cpu_dsu_mux_nb, cpu_dsu_clk);
  * both the +1 on N and P0. Silicon: 974.6 MHz, and the cluster's EXT_DIVP does
  * not divide it -- a park from a /2 OPP still runs at 975 MHz.
  *
- * The DSU keeps the DCXO: its mux has no CPU_BACK_PLL input in our table
- * (encoding 101 is PERI0_600M there, see above); the DSU is handled separately.
+ * The DSU has no CPU_BACK_PLL input; its encoding 101 is PERI0_600M, which
+ * the UM lists as a cluster backup source (5.1.4.1; the primary
+ * source is CPU_DSU_PLL, the others are the 26 MHz DCXO and
+ * CPU_BACK_PLL). The DSU parks there when the DT
+ * wires it: every DSU relock would otherwise hold L3 and the snoop filter of
+ * all eight cores at 26 MHz for the whole relock. 600 MHz is below 780 MHz,
+ * the DSU rate boot0 leaves at DCDC5's 800 mV floor, so the park never runs
+ * the DSU faster than the rail allows. probe() holds the clock enabled, so the
+ * park target cannot be gated underneath the DSU.
  */
 #define A733_CPU_MUX_IDX_BACK_PLL	2
 #define A733_CPU_PARK_MAX_RATE		1014000000UL
+#define A733_DSU_MUX_IDX_PERI0_600M	2
+#define A733_DSU_PARK_RATE		600000000UL
 
 /*
  * How long a cluster really sits on the bypass: PRE_RATE_CHANGE to
@@ -720,9 +732,9 @@ static int sun60i_a733_cpu_ccu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	unsigned int n_min, n_max;
-	unsigned long dcxo_rate, back_rate;
+	unsigned long dcxo_rate, back_rate, peri_rate;
 	void __iomem *reg;
-	struct clk *dcxo;
+	struct clk *dcxo, *peri;
 	unsigned int i;
 	u32 val;
 	int ret;
@@ -791,10 +803,24 @@ static int sun60i_a733_cpu_ccu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		a733_cpu_pll_commons[i]->max_rate = dcxo_rate * n_max;
 	}
 
+	peri = devm_clk_get_optional_enabled(dev, "peri0-600m");
+	if (IS_ERR(peri))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(peri),
+				     "cannot get the peri0-600m park source\n");
+
 	ret = devm_sunxi_ccu_probe(dev, reg, &sun60i_a733_cpu_ccu_desc);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	peri_rate = clk_get_rate(peri);
+	if (peri_rate == A733_DSU_PARK_RATE) {
+		cpu_dsu_mux_nb.bypass_index = A733_DSU_MUX_IDX_PERI0_600M;
+		dev_info(dev, "DSU parks on PERI0_600M during a relock\n");
+	} else {
+		dev_warn(dev, "peri0-600m %s (%lu Hz), DSU parks on the DCXO\n",
+			 peri ? "not at 600 MHz" : "not wired", peri_rate);
+	}
+
 	back_rate = clk_hw_get_rate(&pll_cpu_back_clk.hw);
 	if (clk_hw_is_enabled(&pll_cpu_back_clk.hw) && back_rate &&
 	    back_rate <= A733_CPU_PARK_MAX_RATE) {
